{
  "quest.12E8A5C74F309BD6.title": "What to Do in the Overworld?",
  "quest.12E8A5C74F309BD6.quest_subtitle": "Exploration means leaving and returning reliably",
  "quest.12E8A5C74F309BD6.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: begin a planned Overworld excursion.",
    "",
    "You already know how to mark your home, record coordinates, and protect yourself. You will now combine those skills into a safe exploration routine. Later, this routine will help you find Villages and meet their inhabitants.",
    "",
    "This path is an additional Overworld lesson. It does not block the Nether, Stronghold, or End. Follow it at your own pace.",
    "",
    "Exploring is not the same as walking onward without a plan. Establish a return route before departure, check supplies along the way, and turn around while returning is still easy.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after understanding that difference and deciding to prepare a short daytime excursion first.",
  ],
  "task.23F9B6D85041ACE7.title": "I plan the outward and return routes together",

  "quest.34FAC7E96152BDF8.title": "Pack for a Day Trip",
  "quest.34FAC7E96152BDF8.quest_subtitle": "The return route, tools, and reserves belong together before departure",
  "quest.34FAC7E96152BDF8.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: assemble safe basic equipment for an Overworld excursion.",
    "",
    "Sleep in your Bed at home at least once and leave it there. Check the home coordinates recorded outside the world and your Lodestone Compass. A Compass still does not replace a safe route around cliffs or Water.",
    "",
    "Bring a Pickaxe for stone, an Axe for wood, and a Shovel for soft ground. Wear at least Iron or better Armour, put the Shield in your offhand, and carry eight cooked foods.",
    "",
    "Also pack 16 Torches and 32 Cobblestone. Cobblestone is a visible marker, short safe step, or emergency wall—not an invitation to bridge risky ravines.",
    "",
    "Leave at least eight inventory slots empty. Store ores, rare loot, and anything else you do not need in a Chest at home. One death should not risk your entire collection as well.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when the Bed and route home are checked, all three suitable tools are packed, and at least eight slots are free. The four item tasks complete automatically.",
  ],
  "task.451BD8FA7263CE09.title": "Hold 1 Shield in the inventory",
  "task.562CE90B8374DF1A.title": "Hold 8 cooked foods in the inventory at the same time",
  "task.673DFA1C9485E02B.title": "Hold 16 Torches in the inventory at the same time",
  "task.704E0B2DA596F13C.title": "Hold 32 Cobblestone in the inventory at the same time",
  "task.05AF1C3EB6A7024D.title": "Bed, route home, tools, and empty slots are checked",

  "quest.16B02D4FC7B8135E.title": "Depart in Daylight",
  "quest.16B02D4FC7B8135E.quest_subtitle": "The first excursion starts shortly after morning and ends early enough",
  "quest.16B02D4FC7B8135E.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: leave home in good daylight while keeping the return in mind.",
    "",
    "Sleep until morning or wait safely for the Sun to rise. Do not begin at dusk. A thunderstorm can make daytime dark and dangerous as well, so postpone this first practice excursion when one occurs.",
    "",
    "Turn around after short sections and look at the return route. Notice distinctive hills, groups of trees, shore shapes, or your own sparse Cobblestone markers. Record intermediate coordinates when making a major change of direction if needed.",
    "",
    "Turn back before the Sun is low or before food, Torches, or empty inventory slots run short. An early return is good planning, not a failed excursion.",
    "",
    "Remain within sight of home for this step. Set the checkmark after walking one short safe section and returning to the entrance.",
  ],
  "task.27C13E50D8C9246F.title": "Walked a short daytime section and returned safely",

  "quest.38D24F61E9DA3570.title": "Craft a Boat",
  "quest.38D24F61E9DA3570.quest_subtitle": "Five matching Wooden Planks open safe water routes",
  "quest.38D24F61E9DA3570.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: craft a Boat or Bamboo Raft.",
    "",
    "Open the Crafting Table. Leave the top row empty. Put one Wooden Plank in the left and right slots of the middle row, then fill the entire bottom row with three more Planks of the same wood type. The shape resembles a U.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/boat_recipe.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Boats made from Oak, Spruce, Birch, Jungle, Acacia, Dark Oak, Mangrove, Cherry, or Pale Oak count. Bamboo Planks make a Bamboo Raft in the same shape, which also counts.",
    "",
    "A Boat is fast and useful on Water but moves only very slowly on land. Take it only to a safe, accessible shore near home for now.",
  ],
  "task.49E35072FAEB4681.title": "Own an ordinary Boat or Bamboo Raft",

  "quest.5AF461830BFC5792.title": "Board, Steer, and Leave",
  "quest.5AF461830BFC5792.quest_subtitle": "The Boat remains a tool that you take home again",
  "quest.5AF461830BFC5792.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: practise every important Boat control at a safe shore.",
    "",
    "Hold the Boat in your main hand and right-click calm Water to place it. Right-click the placed Boat again to board it. W moves forward, A and D steer left and right, and S moves backward.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/boat_controls.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Do not enter waterfalls, Lava, unknown deep caves, or an ocean. Practise parallel to a safe shore first so you can reach land at any time.",
    "",
    "Press Shift to leave the Boat. Dismount only at a flat, safe place; the game places you beside the Boat. An empty Boat can drift away on Water.",
    "",
    "Attack the empty Boat with the left mouse button until it drops as an item, then collect it again. Set the checkmark only after placing, boarding, steering, leaving, and retrieving the Boat.",
  ],
  "task.6B0572941C0D68A3.title": "Tried every Boat control and collected the Boat again",

  "quest.7C1683A52D1E79B4.title": "Return to the Same Shore",
  "quest.7C1683A52D1E79B4.quest_subtitle": "The first water journey ends at its known starting point",
  "quest.7C1683A52D1E79B4.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: travel one short known route and return with the Boat.",
    "",
    "Mark a flat boarding place near home and check its coordinates. Travel about 100 blocks parallel to the known shore in daylight. Do not cross a large open ocean for this exercise.",
    "",
    "Turn around before the shore becomes confusing. Return to the marker, leave safely, and collect the Boat again. Briefly check the inventory and route home afterwards.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark at the original shore with the Boat back in your inventory.",
    "",
    "Reward: 5 experience points for a complete outward-and-return journey. In the next section, the same routine will be used to deliberately search for a Village.",
  ],
  "task.0D2794B63E2F8AC5.title": "Returned to the marked starting shore with the Boat",

  "quest.2F49B6D81E50AC73.title": "Search for a Village with a Return Route",
  "quest.2F49B6D81E50AC73.quest_subtitle": "Several short daytime stages are safer than one endless search",
  "quest.2F49B6D81E50AC73.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: discover a Village without abandoning the route home.",
    "",
    "Villages generate only in suitable areas and not at regular distances. Finding none on the first short excursion is normal. Never continue until darkness or empty supplies force the return.",
    "",
    "Choose one direction, record it beside the home coordinates, and explore in daylight. Follow visible terrain lines such as a shore or broad valley. A Boat can speed up rivers and coasts; use safe open routes on land.",
    "",
    "Turn around regularly and inspect how the return route looks from that direction. Record intermediate coordinates at every major turn. Do not depend on individual Torches that may disappear among trees or hills.",
    "",
    "Return home when the Sun is clearly descending, half the food or Torches are gone, or orientation no longer feels reliable. Begin another stage the next morning.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark only after seeing several connected buildings or Villagers from a safe distance. Do not immediately run inside.",
  ],
  "task.305AC7E92F61BD84.title": "Discovered a possible Village from a safe distance",

  "quest.416BD8FA3072CE95.title": "Recognise the Village",
  "quest.416BD8FA3072CE95.quest_subtitle": "Buildings, paths, and inhabitants form one shared place",
  "quest.416BD8FA3072CE95.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: check in daylight whether you have really found a Village.",
    "",
    "A Village usually consists of several generated buildings and paths. Villagers live there; Beds, workstations, small farms, and a Bell are also common. An Iron Golem may guard the Village, but one is not always visible or present.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/village_overview.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "Villages look different in different landscapes. Houses may use other materials and roofs, while paths can break or shift on steep terrain. One house, well, or path alone therefore does not prove that a Village is present.",
    "",
    "Remain outside the buildings at first and observe the area. Do not enter in darkness, and do not attack a Villager or Iron Golem. Do not open a Chest or remove a Bed or workstation yet.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after recognising at least two of these features together: several buildings, paths, Villagers, farms, a Bell, or an Iron Golem.",
  ],
  "task.527CE90B4183DFA6.title": "Recognised several clear Village features",

  "quest.638DFA1C5294E0B7.title": "Secure the Village Location",
  "quest.638DFA1C5294E0B7.quest_subtitle": "Coordinates and a return route come before meeting the inhabitants",
  "quest.638DFA1C5294E0B7.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: make the discovered Village reliably findable again.",
    "",
    "Stand at a visible edge of the Village and record X, Y, and Z outside the world. Add a short description such as ‘Village by the river’ or ‘Village beyond the Birch forest’ so the numbers remain identifiable later.",
    "",
    "Mark the safe approach sparingly with a Sign, small Cobblestone marker, or several Torches. Do not build in the middle of a Village path or block a door. If you arrived by Boat, record the safe landing place as well and either collect the Boat or leave it clearly visible on land.",
    "",
    "Check the first section of the return route afterwards. If darkness approaches, return home and visit again the next morning. The inhabitant lesson does not require staying through the night.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when the Village coordinates and description are recorded and the safe return route or landing place is recognisable.",
    "",
    "Reward: 5 experience points for discovering a Village that you can also find again.",
  ],
  "task.749E0B2D63A5F1C8.title": "Recorded the Village coordinates and marked the return route",

  "quest.14C9E72A5B603DF8.title": "Behave Carefully in the Village",
  "quest.14C9E72A5B603DF8.quest_subtitle": "Meet the inhabitants without harming them or disrupting their routine",
  "quest.14C9E72A5B603DF8.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: move safely and respectfully through the Village.",
    "",
    "Do not attack a Villager or the Iron Golem. A Golem protects the Village and may retaliate after an attack. Do not continue fighting if that happens: run away, gain distance, and return carefully later.",
    "",
    "Leave Beds and workstations where they are. Do not open a Village Chest yet or harvest an entire field. These things support the inhabitants’ routine and will make more sense in later lessons.",
    "",
    "Right-clicking the Bell rings it. The sound can send Villagers into their houses. Try it no more than once, and do not block doors or paths.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after observing the Village without attacking an inhabitant or removing one of its important blocks.",
  ],
  "task.25DAF83B6C714E09.title": "Explored the Village carefully and respectfully",

  "quest.36EB094C7D825F1A.title": "Recognise Professions and Workstations",
  "quest.36EB094C7D825F1A.quest_subtitle": "The workstation reveals what an adult Villager can offer",
  "quest.36EB094C7D825F1A.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: find an adult Villager with a profession and the matching workstation.",
    "",
    "An unemployed adult Villager can claim an available, reachable workstation during the day. Their clothing changes to match the profession; opening the trading screen also shows the profession.",
    "",
    "Examples: Composter = Farmer, Lectern = Librarian, Blast Furnace = Armorer, and Brewing Stand = Cleric. You do not need to craft or move a block for this lesson.",
    "",
    "Baby Villagers cannot trade yet. An adult Villager wearing green is a Nitwit and will not take a profession.",
    "",
    "Before the first trade, a Villager may lose the profession again if the workstation is removed. After a completed trade, the profession and unlocked offers remain. Leave the Village workstations in place.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark after recognising one employed Villager and the matching workstation.",
  ],
  "task.47FC1A5D0E936B2C.title": "Recognised a Villager and the matching workstation",

  "quest.580D2B6E1FA47C3D.title": "Read the Trading Screen",
  "quest.580D2B6E1FA47C3D.quest_subtitle": "Costs on the left, result on the right, and profession experience",
  "quest.580D2B6E1FA47C3D.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: open the trading screen of an adult Villager with a profession and understand one offer.",
    "",
    "Right-click the Villager to open the trading screen. The offers appear on the left. Required items go into the input slots; the item you receive appears in the result slot on the right.",
    "",
    "{image:firsttorch:textures/questpics/villager_trading.png width:300 height:169 align:center}",
    "",
    "The image shows only an example: 20 Wheat are exchanged for one Emerald. The Villager’s actual offers are authoritative and may look different.",
    "",
    "Emeralds are the main trading item used by Villagers. They are not a universal currency for every part of Minecraft.",
    "",
    "The bar at the top shows the Villager’s profession experience. Trading can raise their level and unlock more offers.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you can identify the cost and result of one offer. You do not need to buy anything yet.",
  ],
  "task.691E3C7F20B58D4E.title": "Understood the cost and result of a trade offer",

  "quest.7A2F4D801C639E5F.title": "Complete Your First Trade",
  "quest.7A2F4D801C639E5F.quest_subtitle": "One affordable offer is enough for a beginning",
  "quest.7A2F4D801C639E5F.quest_desc": [
    "Goal: trade with a Villager for the first time. This is detected automatically.",
    "",
    "Choose an offer with a cost you can spare. Do not spend your last food, important tool, or rare material merely to complete this task.",
    "",
    "Place the requested items into the input slots and take the result from the right-hand slot. That completes the trade.",
    "",
    "An offer can temporarily sell out after several uses. The Villager can restock it at their reachable workstation. Prices and available offers can change.",
    "",
    "Reward: four Torches for the journey home and 5 experience points for your first trade.",
  ],
  "task.0B305E912D74AF60.title": "Completed the first trade with a Villager",
  "reward.1C416FA23E85B071.title": "4 × Torch",
  "reward.2D5270B34F96C182.title": "5 Experience Points",
}
